d in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher J. Bilotto | President, CEO & Managing Trustee | Age 47 | Compensation: $1,886 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Service Properties Trust is a small-cap real estate business with a $740M market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $107M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 467% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 70/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 32% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $50.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Service Properties Trust (NASDAQ:SVC) Stock Gets Downgrade from Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/service-properties-trust-nasdaqsvc-stock-gets-downgrade-from-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794481641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Service Properties Trust $SVC Shares Newly Purchased by DBA Trading LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/service-properties-trust-svc-shares-newly-purchased-by-dba-trading-llc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.967,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Service Properties Trust (NASDAQ:SVC) Stock Price Up 5.5% \u2013 Still a Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/service-properties-trust-nasdaqsvc-stock-price-up-5-5-still-a-buy.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794343273.0,"origin":"tiingo","se